231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 115 0 R
/E (Our current robot simulation system faces several limitations. One major issue is its reliance on RGB cameras and LiDAR, which may struggle in real-world disaster scenarios where smoke, dust, or debris obstruct visibility. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 115 0 R
/E (Then, the system is designed for single-robot operation, that lacking coordination strategies for multi-robot setups, which presents challenges in real-time communication and dynamic task allocation among multiple robots. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 115 0 R
/E (The Gazebo simulation used for testing only provides basic disaster zone scenarios, failing to replicate the complexity of real-world conditions such as unstable terrain or extreme weather. Despite these limitations, the foundational concepts for autonomous disaster response robots have been established, though significant improvements are necessary. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 115 0 R
/E (While the current Behavior Tree structures are functional, they need further refinement, and incorporating advanced algorithms like deep reinforcement learning could improve the robot's adaptability and decision-making capabilities.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
